guamp: the surface cache walks (DC CVAC / DC CIVAC) touch only pages the process still maps (SpringBoard SIGSEGV leaving an app, fin55)

fin55 (live-20261106-092610): SpringBoard died twice, at 1110.3 s leaving Telefono and at 1869.4 s leaving Safari, of SIGSEGV
KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS (code 0xb100001) at the same PC: NativeAdrenoMetal +0x2d660 = "dc civac, x11" in invalidateWrittenSurfaces (0001,
0010), called with completed=true from -[NBCommandBuffer finish] on the bridge's completion pthread; faults 0x118800000 and 0x11fb2e000.
(The exit trace's "IntelligentRouting.framework" is only dyld's first image, not the faulting one: plugin base 0x10a4ef000, found from
the PC, LR and the frame chain.) A written surface's pages, the closing app's snapshot, were no longer mapped at IOSurfaceGetBaseAddress
for the whole IOSurfaceGetAllocSize, although the texture retains the surface, and a DC by VA on an unmapped page faults at EL0.
cleanToCoherency and cleanInvalidateToCoherency now clip each range to the readable regions vm_region_recurse_64 reports (one Mach call
per range) and count what they skip; the first 3 cases go to NBLOG ("surface invalidate skipped N unmapped bytes of base+size", to the
kernel log as a problem). A page unmapped between the region query and the walk can still fault (the window is the walk itself).
Stop-gap without a new addon: guamp-m2v-env=NMB_SURFACE_INVALIDATE=0 (no invalidation at all: 0001's stale switcher previews may come
back). Applies after 0001-0057; the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI (forMappedSpans checked on the host with simulated
regions).

